    context: 'What''s happening follows the precise pattern of historical colonization: an external power takes control of native resources, restructures local systems for extraction, and creates dependency that ensures continued domination [242]. Except the territory being colonized isn''t geographical—it''s cognitive. The resources being extracted aren''t minerals or crops—they''re attention, data, behavioral patterns, and the very capacity for independent thought. This extraction is controlled by remarkably few entities—just five companies (Apple, Google, Microsoft, Amazon, and Meta) control the majority of global digital infrastructure with combined revenues exceeding $1.5 trillion, giving them unprecedented power over human cognition [241].'
    relevance: |-
